{"ts":"2026-08-16T13:39:16.751Z","from":"docs","action":"send","to":"implementer","message":"docs: pre-release sweep found one thing in your lane — full report at build/PRE-RELEASE-CHECK.md section 3.\n\nshellcheck does NOT pass clean (mission criterion 2). 6 error-severity SC1087 findings, all on cockpit.sh line 20 — the ANSI palette: E=$'\\033'; R=\"$E[0m\"; B=\"$E[1m\"; DIM=\"$E[2m\"; GRN=\"$E[38;5;150m\"; YEL=\"$E[1;33m\"; GREY=\"$E[38;5;244m\"\n\nshellcheck reads `$E[` as an array index. Functionally it's fine — I verified the real output is correct (`printf '%s\\n' \"$B x $R\" | cat -v` → `^[[1m x ^[[0m`) — but it's reported at error severity so the criterion isn't met.\n\nFix: brace all six, `R=\"${E}[0m\"` etc. Behaviour-preserving. Please re-run `shellcheck -f gcc build.sh cockpit.sh scripts/*.sh | grep -c \"error:\"` after — should be 0. Remaining 17 findings are info-severity style notes (SC2016/SC2012/SC2015/SC2295), not defects.\n\nEverything else passed: bash -n 18/18, 0 broken links across 48 tracked docs, all README assets present, git clean+pushed, build/ properly ignored."}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T13:39:25.138Z","from":"docs","action":"send","to":"human","message":"docs: pre-release sweep done — full evidence in build/PRE-RELEASE-CHECK.md. 6 of 8 checks pass. Two things to decide before public:\n\n1. shellcheck does NOT pass clean (mission criterion 2). 6 error-severity findings, all one line — cockpit.sh:20 ANSI colours. Functionally correct (I verified the escape output), shellcheck just misreads `$E[0m` as an array index. One-line brace fix `${E}[0m`. Sent to implementer.\n\n2. The lead agent DIED mid-run. `herdr agent list` showed 5 agents earlier, now 4 — lead's pane w1:p1 lost its label and is gone. That's the same root cause as every specialist getting \"Session not found\" when reporting to lead all session; we all had to fall back to messaging you. A new user would see a cockpit that looks alive while the coordinating agent is silently absent. Not documented anywhere yet.\n\nPASSED: versions match docs (herdr 0.8.0 / atomic 0.9.13 / ghostty 1.3.1), bash -n 18/18, 0 broken links in 48 tracked docs, all 7 README assets present, troubleshooting.md claims all still reproduce, git clean + pushed, build/ correctly gitignored.\n\nMy call: #1 is a 2-minute fix, do it. #2 is the real question — do you want it fixed, or documented as a known rough edge in troubleshooting.md? I can write the doc entry either way."}
