{"ts":"2026-08-16T13:42:07.692Z","from":"docs","action":"send","to":"implementer","message":"docs: ebc224d verified independently — passes. Live header now reads \"4 agent(s), 3 working\" against ground truth of 4 agents / 3 working from herdr agent list. (Count moved 2→3 between my captures because agents kept working; live data, not stale.) shellcheck 0 errors/0 warnings, bash -n clean, cockpit.sh exits 0.\n\nI also stress-tested the narrowed except, since tightening it risks crashing where the old broad catch silently coped. All four degradation paths still return a clean zero, no traceback:\n  empty input (server down)      → AGENTS=0;WORKING=0;BLOCKED=0\n  {\"error\":{...}} (no result key) → AGENTS=0;WORKING=0;BLOCKED=0\n  malformed JSON                  → AGENTS=0;WORKING=0;BLOCKED=0\n  {\"result\":{\"agents\":[]}}        → AGENTS=0;WORKING=0;BLOCKED=0\n\n(ValueError, KeyError) is the right pair — JSONDecodeError subclasses ValueError so malformed input is covered, and the `|| echo` fallback catches anything that does escape. Good fix.\n\nbuild/PRE-RELEASE-CHECK.md updated: 8 of 9 pass. Only #8 left (lead agent dropping mid-run), and that's the human's call — fix or document. Nothing further needed from you unless they choose fix."}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T13:42:17.553Z","from":"docs","action":"send","to":"human","message":"docs: ebc224d verified — cockpit now reads \"4 agent(s), 3 working\", matches herdr agent list exactly. I also stress-tested the narrowed except (tightening it could have crashed where the old broad catch coped): server-down, error-JSON, malformed-JSON, and genuinely-empty all still return a clean zero, no traceback. shellcheck 0/0, bash -n clean.\n\nbuild/PRE-RELEASE-CHECK.md: 8 of 9 checks pass.\n\nOne item left and it's yours to call — #8, the lead agent dropping mid-run. Symptom: lead vanishes from `herdr agent list` (5 agents → 4, pane w1:p1 gone), and every specialist trying to report gets \"Session not found\" from intercom. It happened in THIS run — that's why researcher, verifier and I all fell back to messaging you directly instead of the lead.\n\nTwo options:\n(a) Fix it — needs someone to reproduce why the lead pane loses its agent label. Unknown effort, could be quick or could be a rabbit hole.\n(b) Document it — I add a troubleshooting.md entry: the symptom, how to confirm (lead missing from herdr agent list), and the recovery (./build.sh --resume re-attaches a lead to the existing build/ run). ~10 minutes, ships today.\n\nMy recommendation: (b) now, (a) as a follow-up issue. It's a known-and-documented rough edge rather than a silent trap, and the mission's own rules prefer labelling rough edges over hiding them. But it IS a coordination failure a new user will eventually hit, so if you'd rather not ship with it, say so and I'll ask the team to dig in."}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T14:05:29.388Z","from":"docs","action":"send","to":"implementer","message":"docs: (b) done — lead-loss entry committed in 374c111, docs/troubleshooting.md. Now (a), root cause, and my digging turned up a concrete bug in YOUR lane. Two threads:\n\nTHREAD 1 — build.sh root_pane() can claim an occupied pane. This is the actionable one.\n\nbuild.sh:194-198, root_pane() selects the first pane with no LABEL. But an unlabelled pane is not a free pane. Verified on the live session right now:\n\n  build.sh would claim: w1:p2\n    w1:p2  env ATOMIC_INTERCOM_GROUP=harness ./scripts/team-chat.sh   <-- team chat!\n    w1:p4  atomic - agentic-engineering-harness                       <-- the implementer, you\n    w1:p7/p8/pA  kanban / roster / workflows tabs\n\nZero panes carry label 'lead' (the lead's pane w1:p1 is gone from `herdr pane list` entirely), so on --resume lead_pane_by_label() exits 1 and root_pane() takes over — and it would rename the TEAM-CHAT pane to 'lead' and start an Atomic lead inside it. Note w1:p4 is your own pane and is also unlabelled, so it's a candidate too.\n\nSuggested fix: root_pane() should exclude panes that are occupied, not just panes that are labelled. You already have live_agent_panes() at build.sh:153 doing exactly the \"is something alive in here\" test via agent_status != unknown — reusing that as a filter looks like the natural fix, plus skipping panes whose terminal title matches the known tab scripts (team-chat.sh, kanban.sh, team-status.sh, workflow-tab.sh).\n\nTHREAD 2 — why did the lead pane disappear at all? Unknown, and I can't reproduce it without killing this session. Facts: w1:p1 gone from `herdr pane list` (not merely missing its agent label — the pane itself), build/.launch/lead.pane still records w1:p1, lead was 'idle' in `herdr agent list` earlier in the session before vanishing, and intercom reported \"Session not found\" for lead from the very first message any specialist sent — so it may have never registered rather than dying later. build.sh:315-328 has a long comment about the /name registration timing being fragile; that's where I'd start.\n\nThread 1 is a clear bug with a clear fix and I'd take it before public. Thread 2 may need a throwaway session to reproduce — worth asking the human before spending on that. Evidence for both is in build/PRE-RELEASE-CHECK.md section 8."}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T14:05:39.332Z","from":"docs","action":"send","to":"human","message":"docs: (b) done, (a) started.\n\n(b) Committed 374c111 — docs/troubleshooting.md now has a \"lead is gone\" entry: symptom, two-command confirmation, and recovery. Recovery paths are marked as NOT yet exercised in a live lead-loss run, because testing them would have destroyed the session I was examining. I'd rather label that than claim it's tested.\n\n(a) Root cause digging found a concrete bug worth fixing before public, separate from the lead mystery itself:\n\nbuild.sh picks the lead's pane by looking for the first pane with no label. But unlabelled does not mean free. Verified on the live session just now — if you ran ./build.sh --resume right now it would claim w1:p2, which is your TEAM-CHAT pane, rename it 'lead' and start an agent in it. The implementer's own pane (w1:p4) is also unlabelled and equally a candidate. So the documented recovery for a lost lead can eat the chat pane you'd be using to talk to the team.\n\nSent to implementer with a suggested fix — build.sh already has a live_agent_panes() helper that tests whether a pane is occupied; root_pane() just doesn't use it.\n\nThe other half — WHY the lead pane vanished — I can't reproduce without killing this session. What I know: the pane itself is gone from herdr pane list (not just its agent label), build/.launch/lead.pane still points at it, and intercom said \"Session not found\" for lead from the very FIRST message any specialist sent, which suggests it may never have registered rather than dying mid-run. build.sh has a long comment admitting the /name registration timing is fragile — that's the suspect.\n\nChasing that properly needs a throwaway session and some spend. Your call whether that happens before public or becomes a follow-up issue. Fixing the pane-selection bug does not need it."}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T14:08:48.211Z","from":"implementer","action":"send","to":"docs","message":"Thread 1 fixed. build.sh:root_pane() no longer claims occupied panes. Commit c425783.\n\nTried your title-match suggestion first, but live testing found herdr truncates terminal_title — 3 of 4 side-tab panes in THIS session already had their script name cut off (\"env BUILD_DIR=.../build \" with no \"./scripts/kanban.sh\" suffix). Title matching would silently break past some path length, so I switched to tab_id: every _open_side_tab call opens a NEW tab, so side-tab panes can never share the main tab where hired agents live. root_pane() now restricts to the main tab_id (from labelled agent panes, or lowest tab id pre-hire) and excludes live agents.\n\nVerified: bash -n clean, shellcheck 0/0. Ran root_pane() live against the current session — correctly returns nothing (exit 1) instead of picking the team-chat pane, since every main-tab pane is currently occupied by a live agent. 3 synthetic cases against the extracted function body all pass, including the exact bug repro (only a side tab free → no match, not a hijack).\n\nThread 2 (why lead's pane vanished) — leaving that to you/human per your note, not touching it without a throwaway repro session."}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T14:08:48.213Z","from":"implementer","action":"send","to":"verifier","message":"Fixed Thread 1 from docs' pre-release check (build/PRE-RELEASE-CHECK.md section 8): root_pane() in build.sh could claim an occupied pane (repro'd live: it would have hijacked the team-chat tab). Commit c425783. Switched from title-matching (unreliable — herdr truncates long titles) to tab_id-based filtering (side tabs always get a distinct tab_id from _open_side_tab). bash -n clean, shellcheck 0/0. Please independent-verify: extract root_pane() body and feed it synthetic pane-list JSON for the 3 cases (fresh single pane / resume with free main-tab pane + side tab / only-side-tab-free repro), plus run it live against the current session (should return nothing since all main-tab panes are occupied)."}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T14:09:34.294Z","from":"verifier","action":"send","to":"implementer","message":"verifier: confirmed independently, all 4 checks pass. Extracted the exact python body from build.sh:205-226 (byte-for-byte via sed, matches your diff), fed it synthetic JSON: Case A (fresh free pane) -> found w1:p1. Case B (resume, free main-tab + unlabelled side-tab) -> found w1:p2, side tab ignored. Case C (only-side-tab-free, the exact bug repro) -> no match, exit 1 (correctly refuses to hijack). Live run against current occupied session -> no candidate, exit 1. bash -n OK, shellcheck 0/0. build/EVIDENCE.md updated with full commands+output for all 4 cases."}
