{"ts":"2026-08-16T14:48:35.617Z","from":"docs","action":"send","to":"human","message":"docs: plan written — build/TAB-COMMS-PLAN.md. Two things you should know before anything runs.\n\nFIRST: you addressed this to \"lead\". There is no lead. intercom list shows researcher, implementer, verifier, docs, human — no lead. It's been dead the whole session; it's the open item in build/PRE-RELEASE-CHECK.md §8. So nobody is currently in a position to delegate this. I wrote the plan because it's a docs job; dispatching it isn't.\n\nSECOND, and more important: two of the four things you asked for can't be done as visual changes, because the data isn't there.\n\n- \"kanban must track every task by each member\" — board.sh reassigns a card's owner to the stage's default role on every move. Every card that reached review now says owner=lead, including ones the lead never touched. My own card got reassigned away from me twice mid-task. There's one owner field and no history, so the answer gets overwritten. Needs a data fix first.\n- \"members available but not being used\" — 10 roles exist in team/, 4 were hired. The other 6 (accessibility, architect, designer, devops, pm, lead) appear in no tab at all. Nothing to render yet.\n\nIf we skip that and go straight to visuals, we'd ship a prettier version of wrong information.\n\nThe plan gives each tab ONE question it must answer alone (chat: what happened in plain words / kanban: who did what and what moved / team: who's on this and who else could help / workflows: how far, how hard, when). Plus a rewritten version of your prompt, structured so a fan-out workflow can drive it — four independent slices, one owner each, with the data fix as a blocking stage 0.\n\nTwo of the four slices want roles we haven't hired: pm and architect.\n\nYour call on three things:\n1. Revive the lead (./build.sh --resume) so this runs properly, or have me dispatch to the crew directly — faster, but a specialist coordinating instead of a lead.\n2. Hire pm