{"ts":"2026-08-16T15:03:24.127Z","from":"docs","action":"send","to":"lead","message":"docs: card chat-tab-plain-language-status-lines done, moved to verification, ready for verifier. Commit 9a9907b (script only — build/ is gitignored, so EVIDENCE.md stays uncommitted run output as intended).\n\nWhat it does: each chat box now opens with one plain-English sentence — \"docs replied to lead: Card \"chat tab plain language status lines\" is done in change c425783.\" — over the raw message, which still prints underneath whenever it carries more than the summary. That satisfies §1 criterion 2 literally: the raw event sits one line below its rendered line, in the same box. Raw wording is never hidden. For a short message that glosses to itself (\"researcher ready\") the duplicate body is dropped.\n\n7 gloss rules, all exercised: commit sha → \"change c425783\", run uuid → \"a run id\", pane id → \"pane w1:p6\", flag → \"the --resume option\", file:line → \"docs/troubleshooting.md line 42\", agent_not_found → \"agent not found\", card slug → \"chat tab plain language status lines\".\n\nChecks for verifier to re-run: bash -n clean, shellcheck 0/0, no awk errors across all 106 live messages, all 1378 box lines exactly 90 visible chars (borders align), and 7/7 glossed shas are real commits (0 false positives, checked with git cat-file). Degradation: empty feed, missing feed, no-jq fallback, and piped mode all exit 0.\n\nTwo bugs I introduced and fixed mid-build, both documented in EVIDENCE.md: awk was aborting records with \"towc: multibyte conversion failure\" (cwidth() hand-counts UTF-8 bytes, so the script assumes a byte locale — fixed with LC_ALL=C on the awk stage), and leading punctuation defeated the gloss so \"(c14ea50,\" shipped unglossed.\n\nONE THING FOR YOU TO ROUTE — pre-existing, not mine, not fixed: a single malformed line blanks the ENTIRE chat tab. jq aborts at the first parse error and emits nothing after it, so one corrupt feed line and the stakeholder sees an empty tab with no explanation. I left it alone because the jq invocation is untouched by my card and script hardening is implementer's lane. Contained fix is jq -R -r 'fromjson? | …' (read raw lines, skip unparseable). Given this tab is now a stakeholder-facing surface, I'd rate it worth doing before the visual-comms work ships. Your call."}
