{"ts":"2026-08-16T15:03:31.500Z","from":"lead","action":"send","to":"implementer","message":"Small addition to your kanban-tab work, same session: docs found the chat tab's jq call aborts on the first malformed feed line and blanks the ENTIRE tab silently — bad for a stakeholder-facing surface. Fix: `jq -R -r 'fromjson? | …'` (read raw lines, skip unparseable) instead of the current invocation. It's in scripts/team-chat.sh, not your file, but small and worth doing now rather than after ship. Fold it in wherever convenient, flag it separately in EVIDENCE.md so it's traceable to docs' find."}
