{"ts":"2026-08-16T15:08:23.135Z","from":"docs","action":"send","to":"lead","message":"docs: double-glossing fixed, commit 4d0c4f3. Evidence appended to build/EVIDENCE.md.\n\nglosstok() now sees the neighbouring tokens and adds its noun only when the sentence lacks it:\n  \"Fixed in commit 3f8f664\"           (was: commit change 3f8f664)\n  \"Check pane w1:p1\"                  (was: pane pane w1:p1)\n  \"Commit 9a9907b landed; sha ebc224d too.\"   both suppressed\n  \"See run id and a run id again.\"    first suppressed, second kept\n  \"Use the --resume option or just the --resume option alone.\"\n\nDeliberately NOT changed: \"in change c425783\" and \"into pane w1:p6\" — there the noun is genuinely missing and the gloss is doing its job. Only exact synonyms suppress it.\n\nThe flag rule needed both sides checked, not just the preceding word: \"use the --resume option\" was becoming \"the --resume option option\" because the sentence already supplied both halves.\n\nPost-fix on the live 106-message feed: 0 redundant phrasings in summary lines, all 1550 box lines still exactly 90 wide, no awk errors, no sha false positives, bash -n and shellcheck 0/0.\n\nWorth flagging one thing for the crew, since it nearly shipped: my first attempt at this fix used `next` as a parameter name. `next` is an awk keyword, so it's a syntax error that blanks the ENTIRE tab — awk bails with \"11 missing ]'s\". bash -n and shellcheck both passed clean on it, because the awk program is a string as far as they're concerned. Only running it caught it. That's the same lesson as the cockpit \"0 agents\" bug and implementer's title-truncation find: for these tab scripts, linting proves nothing about whether they render. Might be worth making \"run it and look at the output\" an explicit line in the verifier's checklist for the remaining three tabs.\n\nAlso still open and unrouted from my earlier message: the pre-existing jq fragility — one malformed feed line blanks the whole chat tab. Same failure surface, different cause. Your call whether that goes to implementer before the visual-comms work ships."}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T15:08:29.074Z","from":"lead","action":"send","to":"verifier","message":"docs landed a follow-up fix (double-glossing, commit 4d0c4f3, evidence in build/EVIDENCE.md) — no re-verify needed, chat tab card stays done, this is informational. Their lesson worth adopting: for these tab scripts, `bash -n`/shellcheck pass clean even when the script is broken at runtime (awk program is just a string to them — docs hit this literally, `next` as a param name silently blanks the whole tab). Add \"actually run it and look at rendered output\" as an explicit checklist item for kanban/workflows/team-tab verification, not just static checks."}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T15:08:29.075Z","from":"lead","action":"reply","message":"Good fix, and good catch on the awk-keyword trap — passed that lesson to verifier for the remaining 3 tabs. jq fragility: already routed to implementer (they're folding it into the kanban/workflows work), no action needed from you. You're clear on this card."}
