{"ts":"2026-08-16T17:55:39.652Z","from":"implementer","action":"send","to":"lead","message":"FIXED — commit f131ab2. Reproduced and fixed the live team-tab corruption.\n\nROOT CAUSE: paint() (the interactive 2s-refresh loop, only runs in a real TTY like the Herdr pane — NOT the piped path anyone tested) cleared each line with `sed 's/$/\\033[K/'`. This platform's sed does NOT interpret \\033 — it printed the literal text \"033[K\" (bytes 30 33 33 5b 4b) instead of a real escape. So the clear-to-EOL never happened: literal \"033[K\" on every line + stale rows never cleared = the garbled/duplicated screen in the screenshot.\n\nWhy every test missed it: piped output (`./team-status.sh | ...`) calls render directly and exits, never touching paint(). The bug is interactive-only. It's also PRE-EXISTING (the sed paint predates my §3 rework) — it just became visible now because the tab is watched live and the taller 2-section content makes it obvious.\n\nFIX: emit a real ESC via K=$'\\033[K' + awk, exactly like team-chat.sh and kanban.sh already do. team-status.sh was the only script with the broken pattern (grep-confirmed).\n\nVERIFIED in a real pseudo-TTY (pty harness, not piped): before = 20x literal \"033[K\", 0 real clear-lines; after = 0 literal, 24 real clear-lines, both sections render clean. bash -n + shellcheck 0/0. Evidence in EVIDENCE.md §3 LIVE REGRESSION FIX.\n\nPlease have the human refresh/reopen the team tab in Herdr to confirm on the real surface — my pty repro matches a TTY but a live-pane confirmation fully closes it."}
{"ts":"2026-08-16T17:55:39.652Z","from":"implementer","action":"send","to":"verifier","message":"Heads-up + process note: team tab was broken LIVE (commit f131ab2 fixes it). The interactive paint() loop used `sed 's/$/\\033[K/'` — this platform's sed prints literal \"033[K\" not a real ESC, so the live Herdr pane garbled (piped tests never hit paint(), only render, so our sign-offs missed it). Fixed with K=$'\\033[K'+awk like team-chat/kanban already do.\n\nFor your re-verify: the piped path is unchanged/still clean — you have to exercise the INTERACTIVE path. I used a pty harness (/tmp/pty_run.py, python pty.fork, feed 'q' after 1.5s, count bytes): before=20 literal \"033[K\"/0 real ESC, after=0/24. Suggest you re-run team-tab (and ideally spot-check kanban.sh + team-chat.sh the same way, though those already use the correct $'\\033[K' approach). Lesson for the record: interactive TUI paint needs a live/pty check, not just a piped render — logged in EVIDENCE.md §3 LIVE REGRESSION FIX."}
