{"ts":"2026-08-16T17:58:51.169Z","from":"verifier","action":"send","to":"lead","message":"verifier: CONFIRMED — fix verified in a real pty AND on the live pane. §3 regression CLOSED. (1) PTY: wrote my own harness (pty.fork + real window size via TIOCSWINSZ + feed 'q' + count literal \"033[\" vs real 0x1b bytes), not implementer's, and validated it against a known-bad control FIRST — a harness that can't detect the bug proves nothing. Broken b2afb11: 20 literal / 0 real ESC[K → FAIL. Fixed HEAD f131ab2: 0 literal / 24 real ESC[K → PASS. Independently reproduces implementer's 20/0→0/24 numbers. (2) ALL FOUR TABS under pty 120x40: team-status 0, kanban 0, workflow-tab 0, team-chat 6 — but the team-chat 6 are a FALSE POSITIVE: they're chat message bodies quoting the literal string \"033[K\" (this very investigation is in the feed). Verified by dumping surrounding bytes — each sits inside real rendered escapes \\x1b[38;2;...m, so the renderer is correct. Not a defect. (3) YOUR GREP ASK — pattern is isolated, no other script affected: no sed-with-\\033 anywhere in the repo; all four tabs use K=$'\\033[K' ANSI-C quoting; team-chat.sh:346,348 use printf which DOES interpret \\033 correctly. The only remaining \"033\" in a sed context is the explanatory comment at team-status.sh:160. (4) LIVE PANE, after its owner restarted it: `herdr pane read w1:p8 | grep -c '033['` = 0 (was 13), and the full §3 content now renders — hired profiles with status/task, AVAILABLE-NOT-HIRED section, wrapped controls. The human-visible symptom is gone. One harness lesson worth recording: my first pty attempt didn't set a window size, and kanban.sh crashed with \"division by 0\" at line 201 because tput cols returned nothing — that was MY harness artifact, not a kanban bug (it renders fine with a proper winsize and in the real pane). Worth knowing that team-status.sh has a `|| echo 100` fallback there and kanban.sh doesn't, but I'm not raising it: no real pane lacks a size. Full writeup in build/EVIDENCE.md §3 REGRESSION → FINAL VERIFICATION."}
